! ======================================================================
! test_v094_h2o_tddft_pcm -- TDDFT + PCM (LR solvent response)
!
! Water B3LYP/STO-3G in C-PCM water, 3 singlets + 3 triplets,
! NONEQUILIBRIUM solvation (default): the response kernel is built at
! the optical permittivity eps_inf = n^2 = 1.7756 (solvent table),
! the ground state at the static eps = 78.3553.
!
! Reference (v0.94.0, 1 thread, reference BLAS; confirmed under the
! v0.95.0 per-quartet HRR dispatch: ground state and all six
! excitation energies reproduce at print precision.  The TRIPLET
! per-state E_total values move in the 7th decimal with ERI
! routing -- the finite-difference cross-spin kernel amplifies
! last-bit input changes; the E_exc references below stand):
!   PCM ground state:  Total energy  -75.281981388350
!   LR-PCM solvent response: NONEQUILIBRIUM (eps_dyn = 1.7756)
!   Singlets, E_exc (Ha):  0.438448   0.520641   0.542005
!   Triplets, E_exc (Ha):  0.366400   0.449967   0.474500
!
! Physics checks encoded by these numbers:
!   * the singlet kernel is STABILIZING relative to the pure
!     orbital-shift picture (Kpcm diagonal < 0);
!   * triplets carry NO direct solvent-response kernel (spin-summed
!     transition charge density vanishes) -- they shift from the gas
!     values (0.355902 / 0.438423 / 0.466438, test_v087) only through
!     the PCM ground-state orbitals;
!   * with %eps 1.00001 and %eps_optical 1.00001 all six excitation
!     energies collapse to the gas values of test_v087 exactly at
!     print precision;
!   * %tddft_pcm equilibrium (kernel at the static eps) lowers the
!     singlets further: 0.438295 / 0.520593 / 0.539968 Ha;
!   * %tddft_selftest on cross-checks the assembled (A+B) column,
!     INCLUDING the PCM kernel, against an independent AO-side
!     response build to machine precision (~2e-14).
! ======================================================================
%method  B3LYP
%basis   sto-3g
%job     energy
%charge  0
%mult    1
%tddft   3
%tddft_multiplicity both
%pcm     cpcm
%solvent water
%geom angstrom
O    0.000000    0.000000    0.117300
H    0.000000    0.757200   -0.469200
H    0.000000   -0.757200   -0.469200
*end
